    "help": {
      "format": "restructuredtext",
      "content": "\n\n========\nSynopsis\n========\n\nCombines two datasets into a single paired collection (forward + reverse).\n\n===========\nDescription\n===========\n\nThis tool takes two individual datasets and packages them into a ``paired`` collection, labeling the first as **forward** and the second as **reverse**.\n\nThis is the inverse of **Unzip collection**, which splits a pair back into two separate datasets.\n\n========\nExamples\n========\n\n**Zip two datasets into a pair**\n\nInputs::\n\n Input 1 (forward):  reads_R1.fastq\n Input 2 (reverse):  reads_R2.fastq\n\nOutput ``paired`` collection::\n\n Paired: \"reads (zipped)\"\n\n   forward  →  reads_R1.fastq\n   reverse  →  reads_R2.fastq\n\n-------\n\n.. image:: ${static_path}/images/tools/collection_ops/zip.svg\n  :alt: Zip two datasets into a paired collection\n  :width: 500\n\n-------\n\n.. class:: infomark\n\nThis tool will create new history datasets copied from your input collections but your quota usage will not increase.\n\n  "
    }
  },
